In a previous article, mackenzi@McRCIM.McGill.EDU (Paul Mackenzie) says:

>
>This may be a stupid question, but do levels in Hell have stairs down?
>I am in the level below the castle, and cannot find stairs down, even though
>I have been everywhere on the level (as far as I know - I may have missed 
>somewhere).  Somehow I have a resist-magic intrinsic, so the level teleports 
>don't work.

	Hell only has up staircases. If you are magic-resistant, you
are likely wearing a cloak of magic resistance or gray dragon scale
mail, which you should take off before stepping onto a level teleporter.
As far as I know, magic-resistance can only be gained by wearing one
of those two pieces of armor. (The WCST spoilers make no mention
of any permanently gainable magic resistance intrinsic.)
	You can only get to hell by teleporting, and you need the
teleport control intrinsic. Level teleporters are the most obvious
and probably the easiest way, but cursed scrolls of teleport will
also work. Being confused while reading a scroll of teleport is
probably the most complicated way of doing it, but what the heck,
its there.

 
